-- title:
--   Theorem 6.3 — Weyl criterion (odd prime $p$): surjective $*$-homomorphism iff $A^{\mathsf T}\Omega_{m_A}A=B^{\mathsf T}\Omega_{m_B}B$, $K_A\subseteq K_B$, $\zeta_A=\zeta_B$
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, $\omega=e^{2\pi i/p}$, $W_m(x,z)=\omega^{x\cdot z/2}\bigotimes_jX_p^{x_j}Z_p^{z_j}$ the Weyl operators (exponents in $\mathbb F_p$). Choose nonzero Weyl directions $w_i\in\mathbb F_p^{2m_A}$, $v_i\in\mathbb F_p^{2m_B}$ and phases $r_i^A,r_i^B\in\mathbb F_p$, and set $a_i(\xi)=\omega^{\xi r_i^A}W_{m_A}(\xi w_i)$, $b_i(\xi)=\omega^{\xi r_i^B}W_{m_B}(\xi v_i)$ for $\xi\in\mathbb F_p$, $\mathcal A=C^*(I_A,a_i(\xi):i\in[s],\xi\in\mathbb F_p)$, $\mathcal B$ likewise, $A=[w_1\cdots w_s]$, $B=[v_1\cdots v_s]$, $K_A=\ker A$, $K_B=\ker B$ over $\mathbb F_p$, and $W_L(c)=a_1(c_1)\cdots a_s(c_s)$ (resp. $b$), $W_L(c)=\zeta_L(c)I_L$ for $c\in K_L$.
--
--   1. The assignment $a_i(\xi)\mapsto b_i(\xi)$ ($i\in[s]$, $\xi\in\mathbb F_p$) extends to a surjective unital $*$-homomorphism $\pi_p:\mathcal A\to\mathcal B$ if and only if
--   $$A^{\mathsf T}\Omega_{m_A}A=B^{\mathsf T}\Omega_{m_B}B,\qquad K_A\subseteq K_B,\qquad\zeta_A(c)=\zeta_B(c)\ \ (c\in K_A),$$
--   where $\Omega_m=\begin{pmatrix}0&-I_m\\I_m&0\end{pmatrix}$.
--   2. For the matched Hamiltonians $H_A^{(p)}=E_cI_A+\sum_i\sum_{\xi\in\Lambda_i}\lambda_{i,\xi}a_i(\xi)$, $H_B^{(p)}=E_cI_B+\sum_i\sum_{\xi\in\Lambda_i}\lambda_{i,\xi}b_i(\xi)$, with nonempty symmetric symbol sets $\Lambda_i=-\Lambda_i\subseteq\mathbb F_p^\times$, $\lambda_{i,-\xi}=\overline{\lambda_{i,\xi}}$ and $E_c\in\mathbb R$, every such map satisfies
--   $$\pi_p(H_A^{(p)})=H_B^{(p)},\qquad\pi_p(p_0(H_A^{(p)}))=p_0(H_B^{(p)})$$
--   for every polynomial $p_0$.
--
--   This extends the homomorphism criterion to prime-dimensional qudits and occupation-truncated bosonic systems, where the powers along one Weyl direction form a single $\mathbb F_p$-valued coordinate.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: p an odd prime → [Fact p.Prime] and p ≠ 2; reason: same primes
--   - encoding: A = C∗(I_A, aᵢ(ξ) : i ∈ [s], ξ ∈ F_p), π_p : A → B surjective unital ∗-homomorphism with π_p(aᵢ(ξ)) = bᵢ(ξ) → familyAlg (weylGen rA wA), the ∗-subalgebra generated by the family indexed by Fin s × ZMod p; π : familyAlg … →⋆ₐ[ℂ] familyAlg … with π (familyGen a (i, ξ)) = familyGen b (i, ξ) and Function.Surjective π; reason: in finite dimension the generated ∗-subalgebra is the generated C∗-algebra (App. E, p.85)
--   - encoding: ω^{x·z/2} with exponents in F_p; labels (x, z) ∈ F_p^{2m} → ω^{k.val} for k : ZMod p with /2 = · (2 : ZMod p)⁻¹; labels as pairs (Fin m → ZMod p) × (Fin m → ZMod p), columns of the label matrix x then z (Fin m ⊕ Fin m); reason: ω^p = 1, so ω^k is well defined on F_p; same operators and matrices
--   - encoding: ζ_A(c) = ζ_B(c) for c ∈ K_A, where W_L(c) = ζ_L(c) I for c ∈ K_L → ∀ c ∈ K_A, ∀ ζ : ℂ, W_A(c) = ζ • 1 → W_B(c) = ζ • 1; reason: for c ∈ K_A the word W_A(c) is scalar, so ζ_A(c) is the unique ζ with W_A(c) = ζI (the matrix algebras are nonzero); the implication then says W_B(c) = ζ_A(c)I, i.e. ζ_B(c) = ζ_A(c)
--   - encoding: Λᵢ = −Λᵢ ⊆ F_p^× nonempty, λ_{i,−ξ} = λ_{i,ξ}^∗, polynomials p₀ → Λ i : Finset (ZMod p) nonempty, 0 ∉ Λ i, closed under negation; lam i (−ξ) = star (lam i ξ) for ξ ∈ Λ i; p₀ : Polynomial ℂ evaluated by Polynomial.aeval; reason: Lean convention; same Hamiltonians and identities
-- source:
--   Shang, Stilck França, From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), Theorem 6.3, p.47 (pdf_page 47); setting eqs. (225)–(226), p.43, and (246)–(259), pp.46–47; proof Proposition E.4, pp.89–90

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RelDecoding_Supplement_labelKer
import Definitions.Def_RelDecoding_Supplement_weylGen

set_option autoImplicit false
open scoped Matrix

namespace RelDecoding.Supplement

/-- **Theorem 6.3 (Homomorphisms between Weyl-generated algebras).** Let `p` be an odd prime,
`wᵢ ∈ F_p^{2m_A}`, `vᵢ ∈ F_p^{2m_B}` nonzero Weyl directions and `rᵢᴬ, rᵢᴮ ∈ F_p` phases, with
field-symbol generators `aᵢ(ξ) = ω^{ξrᵢᴬ} W_{m_A}(ξwᵢ)`, `bᵢ(ξ) = ω^{ξrᵢᴮ} W_{m_B}(ξvᵢ)` (248),
`A = C∗(I_A, aᵢ(ξ) : i ∈ [s], ξ ∈ F_p)`, `B` likewise (253), label matrices `A = [w₁ ⋯ w_s]`,
`B = [v₁ ⋯ v_s]`, kernels `K_A`, `K_B` over `F_p` and words `W_L(c) = a₁(c₁)⋯a_s(c_s)`
(`= ζ_L(c) I_L` for `c ∈ K_L`). The assignment `aᵢ(ξ) ↦ bᵢ(ξ)` (`i ∈ [s]`, `ξ ∈ F_p`) (260) extends
to a surjective unital ∗-homomorphism `π_p : A → B` if and only if
`AᵀΩ_{m_A}A = BᵀΩ_{m_B}B`, `K_A ⊆ K_B`, `ζ_A(c) = ζ_B(c)` (`c ∈ K_A`) (261). For the matched
Hamiltonians `H_A^{(p)} = E_c I_A + Σᵢ Σ_{ξ∈Λᵢ} λ_{i,ξ} aᵢ(ξ)`, `H_B^{(p)}` likewise, with
`Λᵢ = −Λᵢ ⊆ F_p^×` nonempty, `λ_{i,−ξ} = λ_{i,ξ}^*`, `E_c ∈ ℝ` (252), this gives
`π_p(H_A^{(p)}) = H_B^{(p)}` and `π_p(p₀(H_A^{(p)})) = p₀(H_B^{(p)})` for every polynomial `p₀` (262).

Shang, Stilck França, *From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial
Transduction via Relative Decoding*, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…),
Theorem 6.3, p.47 (setting eqs. (225)–(226), p.43, and (246)–(259), pp.46–47; proof Proposition E.4,
pp.89–90).

**Formalization Note.** `W_m` is `weylOp` on the basis `Fin m → ZMod p`; the generators form the
family `weylGen r w : Fin s × ZMod p → Matrix`, and `A = familyAlg (weylGen rA wA)`. `π_p` is a
unital ∗-homomorphism `A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] B` with `π_p(a_{(i,ξ)}) = b_{(i,ξ)}` for every `(i, ξ)` and
`Function.Surjective π_p`. Labels are pairs `(x, z)`, read as columns of `F_p^{2m}` X-part first.
The phase condition is encoded as: for `c ∈ K_A`, `W_A(c) = ζI_A` implies `W_B(c) = ζI_B`.
Polynomials are complex, `p₀ ∈ ℂ[X]`. -/
theorem theorem_6_3 {p mA mB s : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] (hp : p ≠ 2)
    (wA : Fin s → (Fin mA → ZMod p) × (Fin mA → ZMod p)) (rA : Fin s → ZMod p)
    (wB : Fin s → (Fin mB → ZMod p) × (Fin mB → ZMod p)) (rB : Fin s → ZMod p)
    (hwA : ∀ i, wA i ≠ 0) (hwB : ∀ i, wB i ≠ 0) :
    ((∃ π : familyAlg (weylGen rA wA) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] familyAlg (weylGen rB wB),
        (∀ q, π (familyGen (weylGen rA wA) q) = familyGen (weylGen rB wB) q) ∧
          Function.Surjective π) ↔
      ((labelMatrix fun i => pairVec (wA i))ᵀ * omegaForm mA p *
            labelMatrix (fun i => pairVec (wA i)) =
          (labelMatrix fun i => pairVec (wB i))ᵀ * omegaForm mB p *
            labelMatrix (fun i => pairVec (wB i)) ∧
        labelKer (fun i => pairVec (wA i)) ≤ labelKer (fun i => pairVec (wB i)) ∧
        ∀ c ∈ labelKer (fun i => pairVec (wA i)), ∀ ζ : ℂ,
          symbolWord (weylGen rA wA) c = ζ • 1 → symbolWord (weylGen rB wB) c = ζ • 1)) ∧
    ∀ π : familyAlg (weylGen rA wA) →⋆ₐ[ℂ] familyAlg (weylGen rB wB),
      (∀ q, π (familyGen (weylGen rA wA) q) = familyGen (weylGen rB wB) q) →
      Function.Surjective π →
      ∀ (Ec : ℝ) (Λ : Fin s → Finset (ZMod p)) (lam : Fin s → ZMod p → ℂ),
        (∀ i, (Λ i).Nonempty) → (∀ i, (0 : ZMod p) ∉ Λ i) →
        (∀ i, ∀ ξ ∈ Λ i, -ξ ∈ Λ i) →
        (∀ i, ∀ ξ ∈ Λ i, lam i (-ξ) = star (lam i ξ)) →
        ((π ((Ec : ℂ) • (1 : familyAlg (weylGen rA wA)) +
              ∑ i, ∑ ξ ∈ Λ i, lam i ξ • familyGen (weylGen rA wA) (i, ξ)) :
              Matrix (Fin mB → ZMod p) (Fin mB → ZMod p) ℂ) =
            (Ec : ℂ) • (1 : Matrix (Fin mB → ZMod p) (Fin mB → ZMod p) ℂ) +
              ∑ i, ∑ ξ ∈ Λ i, lam i ξ • weylGen rB wB (i, ξ)) ∧
        ∀ p₀ : Polynomial ℂ,
          ((π (Polynomial.aeval ((Ec : ℂ) • (1 : familyAlg (weylGen rA wA)) +
                ∑ i, ∑ ξ ∈ Λ i, lam i ξ • familyGen (weylGen rA wA) (i, ξ)) p₀) :
                Matrix (Fin mB → ZMod p) (Fin mB → ZMod p) ℂ) =
            Polynomial.aeval ((Ec : ℂ) • (1 : Matrix (Fin mB → ZMod p) (Fin mB → ZMod p) ℂ) +
              ∑ i, ∑ ξ ∈ Λ i, lam i ξ • weylGen rB wB (i, ξ)) p₀) := by sorry

end RelDecoding.Supplement
